\f1\fs22 Picture your grandmother. Now give her glossy white hair spun with gold. Let her teeth be flawless, her complexion unblemished, her blue eyes clear and calculating. Dress her in a season\'92s designer business suit, drape her in the most sumptuous cuddly shawl. She\'92s slender, and lithe, all the way down to her patent leather lawn-bowling shoes.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable><!$Scr_Ps::0><$Scr_Ps::1>
\f1\fs22 Now, straighten her spine, square her shoulders, transform her carriage and deportment. Think just a hint of Candice Bergen, a glint of Gloria Steinem, maybe a little Jane Fonda, and a great deal of Daphne du Maurier.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Ah, there you almost have Eloise Shakti. All that remains is to assign her an expensively and ascetically clad entourage who remind you of dentists; or international assassins; or perhaps both.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl220\sb220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 <!$Scr_Ps::1><$Scr_Ps::0>
\f1\fs22 Sarah waited in the mansion\'92s parlour while Nancy showed Eloise and her international dentist-assassins in. After exchanging pleasantries, Eloise sat, posture-perfect, letting her suit whisper \'93expensive\'94 so quietly that only accountants and undertakers could hear, while Sarah pulled herself from slouching uncomfortably on the lounge to a posture fit for royalty.\
