\f1\i0 \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Nancy arrived and served tea and biscuits, of which Eloise ceremonially partook, while her entourage stood like Huon pines in an unheard-of forest. As Nancy left, Eloise nibbled the corner of a biscuit, took an elegant draught of tea, set the cup and saucer down, and warmly said, \'93Hand over the Gyges Disc.\'94 
\f2\i (dearie)
\f1\i0 \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>After several seconds of her bowels turning to ice and her skeleton to chalk, Sarah stammered, \'93What\'92s a Gy\'97\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Sarah\'85 may I call you Sarah? You won\'92t know this, but I\'92ve kept a keen interest in you for many years.\'94 Eloise sipped tea and dabbed her mouth with a napkin. \'93Many, many years. Quite a few more than anyone might give credit for.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>If Sarah was chilled before, Eloise\'92s words froze her to splinters.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93The thing is, I think of you as family. For many reasons\'97some of which I suspect you appreciate very well indeed\'97you are close to my heart. So, I hope we can be on the same side of this, Sarah. Wouldn\'92t you like that too?\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah animated her head enough to nod.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Excellent.\'94 If your grandmother were a snake that could smile, she\'92d smile the way Eloise smiled. \'93The Gyges Disc, which is currently in your possession\'97\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93I \'97 I don\'92t have\'85\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Family doesn\'92t lie to family, does it, Sarah? I know you have the disc. It\'92s a simple matter of following the earthquakes. Your lover, Anthony Chantara, had it\'97\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93He\'92s not my\'97\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Sarah, my love, this will go exactly the same way, whether you interrupt or not. Shall we save us both the tedium?\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah blushed and crammed down her resentment.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93The disc was in the room you shared with Chantara before his arrest.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93I swear, I have no idea\'97\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Eloise hushed Sarah with a decisive palm. She sucked her teeth, pulled her shawl tighter, checked her watch, and seemed to count off semi-seconds with her index finger. Then she snapped her fingers so loudly it sounded like bones breaking, and one of her entourage dropped to the floor. The others stayed rooted in place, paying no attention.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah gasped. \'93You killed her?\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93No, your constant interruptions killed her.\'94 
\f2\i (dearie)
\f1\i0  \'93If you\'92d surrendered the disc in time, I could have saved her.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93You\'92d kill a\'97\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93A contractor, nothing else,\'94 Eloise interjected before Sarah could say something more humanising.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93\'85 to teach me what, exactly?\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93The consequence of wasting my time.\'94 
