\f1\i0 \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93If you think I will respond to such\'97\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Forgive me,\'94 Eloise said. \'93I neglected to introduce my team. The one on the floor is Alexa.\'94 She gestured to the one standing leftmost. \'93This next one is Mike.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Mike swallowed hard.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Shall I go on?\'94 Eloise asked, unfussed.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah felt something diabolically rotten, like acid corroding her insides, concrete in her bones, shards of glass in her head. This must be what it felt like to be beaten. \'93Okay, okay, I\'92ll get it.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Eloise raised her eyebrow.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93It\'92s upstairs, in my room.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Eloise nodded. Sarah ran.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>She returned with a handkerchief, unfolded it, and presented it. Eloise took one look and waved it away in disgust. \'93What have you been doing, blowing your nose on it?\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah stood paralysed. First Eloise killed for the disc, now she shunned it?\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Just put it on the table,\'94 Eloise instructed. Then she called, \'93Mr Stoat.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>A large, bald man entered, wearing an expensive tailored suit that hung from him so badly, it looked like a polyester tablecloth at a royal banquet.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Johnny!\'94 Sarah almost spat. \'93You sold me out!\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Johnny couldn\'92t meet Sarah\'92s eye. He picked up the handkerchief, examined the disc, and folded it away.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Johnny?\'94 Sarah pleaded, feeling truly heartbroken. \'93You work for\'85 this?\'94 Sarah waved at thin air and shook her head.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93I\'92ve worked for one of her subsidiaries for years.\'94 Johnny pocketed the disc. \'93It\'92s not as if it\'92s a secret.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>It may as well have been a secret, for all Sarah cared for Johnny\'92s career.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Eloise, satisfied, rose. \'93Well, there ends the demonstration.\'94 She swept her entourage after her, leaving the fallen one behind\'97someone else\'92s job. \'93Oh, one more thing,\'94 Eloise added, using the old, 
